From b061136cbefb61faf28ee992035aade789c5bc1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:27:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] keyboard: Enter is Circle, Start moves to P, Ctrl skips
 messages

- ps2_pad_keys.h: the keyboard pad map as a header-only function (fake
  keyboard in the tests). Enter, keypad Enter, C and Esc are Circle; Start is
  P; Alt+Enter stays the fullscreen shortcut and presses nothing, also when
  Alt is released first.
- Ctrl (either side) held skips story messages: ga2_framepace skip state,
  fed by the game side (native/compat/ga2_skip.cpp: the ADV scene's update,
  the choice/menu builtin and the ship map's update) and by the pad: Circle
  every other pad frame, only while a story script is on and nothing blocks
  it. Any other button pressed while Ctrl is held disarms until Ctrl is
  released; the system menu and the backlog on the picture (strict colour
  signatures, ps2_mouse_menus) block it too. Scripted pad runs ignore Ctrl.
- tests: pad_keymap_tests.cpp (the keyboard map with a fake keyboard, Alt+Enter, Ctrl).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
